  {
   "name": "Pulse Organ",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "organ",
   "tags": [
    "organ",
    "User PWM",
    "cross-modulated LFOs"
   ],
   "description": "After Oatmeal's organ blergh: a drawbar wave played as a pulse (User PWM), its width pushed open by a slow mod envelope on each chord and slowly modulated, so the drawbars seem to move. Two vibrato-and-pan LFOs modulate each other's depth, so the wobble never repeats, and a short key click starts each note. Low shelves warm the body. Mod wheel: faster LFOs, like a rotor speeding up; aftertouch: drive. Macros: drawbars, click, wobble.",
