  {
   "name": "Solina Phase",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "string machine",
    "phaser",
    "ensemble",
    "vibrato"
   ],
   "description": "A string machine: two saws an octave apart through a soft MG lowpass, a three-voice ensemble chorus, then the rack's phaser sweeping slowly with some feedback. Each chord brightens as it's bowed, the octaves trade places slowly in every note, a vibrato fades in on held notes and each note is a few cents off. Mod wheel: a faster, deeper phaser; aftertouch: brighter, more vibrato. Macros: phase, ensemble, brightness.",
