  {
   "name": "Warm Wool",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "ladder",
    "per-voice drive",
    "analog",
    "PWM"
   ],
   "description": "Soft saturation in front of each note's ladder filter, so the filter rounds off the drive. Osc 2 is a warm harmonic wave played as a pulse (User PWM), its width swept by its own PWM and by a slow per-note LFO, so the harmonics comb and shift inside every note; a shared random LFO makes the fuzz breathe. Each note is tuned and filtered a little differently. Play harder for more fuzz. Mod wheel: resonance; aftertouch: drive and cutoff. Macros: warmth, cutoff, movement.",
