  {
   "name": "Ghost Tide",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "PWM",
    "FM chorus",
    "evolving",
    "filter envelope"
   ],
   "description": "After Oatmeal's ghrutenbngtb: a pulse that opens from nothing into a square as a mod envelope widens it, with a triangle two octaves up fading in alongside, through a filter that starts wide open and closes over four seconds while a wobble on it grows in over the same time, all through a slow FM chorus. Every note is a few cents off, and a random LFO per note moves it around. Mod wheel: a faster wobble; aftertouch: opens the filter back up. Macros: tide, wobble.",
