  {
   "name": "Fuzz Lead",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "lead",
   "tags": [
    "mono",
    "fuzz",
    "guitar amp",
    "convolution",
    "cabinet"
   ],
   "description": "Two detuned saws through a guitar amp (a distortion model: a high-gain amp into a 4×12 cabinet) after the filter, so the amp sees every harmonic and the two saws grind against each other, then a 1×12 cabinet (convolved) blended in for a smaller box. Held notes swell into more gain like an amp feeding back, the pick attack and the beat between the saws change from note to note, and a random LFO wobbles the tone. It starts as a crunch: the mod wheel turns it into full fuzz; aftertouch sweeps a resonant wah in front of the amp. Macros: fuzz, cutoff, cabinet, tone.",
