  {
   "name": "Trill Lead",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "lead",
   "tags": [
    "trill",
    "tempo sync",
    "flanger chorus",
    "evolving"
   ],
   "description": "After Oatmeal's urghlblrugh: a saw and a triangle through a lowpass, with a sixteenth-note square LFO on the pitch whose depth grows over a few seconds, so a held note slowly opens into a whole-tone trill above it, harder notes trilling sooner. A flanging negative-feedback chorus. Mod wheel: the trill right away; aftertouch: brighter. Macros: trill, cutoff.",
