  {
   "name": "Reese Drift",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "reese",
    "unison",
    "drift",
    "SVF",
    "flanger",
    "XY pad"
   ],
   "description": "Two detuned HQ saws with unison and analog drift, through a state-variable filter whose slow LFO morphs it between lowpass and bandpass. A second slow LFO changes how fast the saws beat against each other, and a slow flanger in the rack (with the bass kept mono) adds the jet. The XY pad: X opens the filter, Y adds resonance and drive. Mod wheel: resonance and more bandpass; aftertouch: drive. Macros: growl, drive.",
