  {
   "name": "Wub Bass",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "dubstep",
    "wobble",
    "tempo sync",
    "OTT"
   ],
   "description": "A classic dubstep wobble: detuned saws over a sine sub an octave down, through a driven dirty lowpass that an eighth-note LFO swings open and shut, with the drive after it pumping along. The mod wheel (or macro 1) speeds the wobble up to sixteenths and triplets for the build; the three-band compressor squashes it and a utility keeps the lows mono. Aftertouch: resonance. Macros: wobble rate, depth, drive.",
