  {
   "name": "Growl Bass",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "dubstep",
    "FM",
    "formant",
    "growl"
   ],
   "description": "A growl: a sine phase-modulated by another at the same pitch, its index and a formant filter's vowel both riding a quarter-note LFO and kicking on each note, into a hard clipper (4x oversampled), a second distortion, the three-band compressor and a bass-mono utility. Mod wheel: the growl goes to eighths; aftertouch: more FM. Macros: growl, vowel, rate.",
