  {
   "name": "Yoi Bass",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "dubstep",
    "formant",
    "vowel",
    "pitch envelope"
   ],
   "description": "A yoi bass: a saw and a square an octave down through a formant filter whose vowel jumps on every note while the pitch scoops up from below, a quick 'yoi'. Then a soft drive and the three-band compressor. Every note's vowel starts a little differently; the mod wheel adds a quarter-note vowel wobble, aftertouch more drive. Macros: yoi, vowel, drive.",
