  {
   "name": "Resonator Pluck",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pluck",
   "tags": [
    "voice lane",
    "resonator",
    "osc envelopes",
    "string"
   ],
   "description": "Only a pick goes in: a pulse and a triangle that their own envelopes cut off within a tenth of a second, and a tick of noise, into a resonator in every voice tuned to its note, which rings as the string. Each string rings for its own time and at its own brightness, harder plucks are brighter, high strings ring shorter, and each is tuned a hair apart and placed at its own spot in the stereo field. The amp envelope damps the string when the key is let go. Mod wheel: a longer ring; aftertouch: brighter. Macros: ring, brightness, pick, body.",
