  {
   "name": "Glass Pluck",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pluck",
   "tags": [
    "phase modulation",
    "feedback",
    "digital",
    "OTT"
   ],
   "description": "A glassy digital pluck: a sine phase-modulating itself, its feedback struck high on every note (harder with velocity, less for high notes) and falling back towards a pure tone, over a quiet sine an octave up. Each pluck's feedback is cast a little differently. A light OTT, a dotted-eighth delay and a small plate. Mod wheel: vibrato; aftertouch: more feedback. Macros: glass, space.",
