  {
   "name": "Brassy Oats",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "brass",
   "tags": [
    "brass",
    "per-voice drive",
    "ladder",
    "EQ",
    "section"
   ],
   "description": "Synth brass: a ladder with a slow-attack filter envelope and a soft drive on each voice, so loud chords get raspy without turning to mush. Each note's pitch scoops up slightly and each player is a few cents and a shade of brightness apart, with a little breath wavering the filter; a vibrato comes in on long notes. The EQ lifts the upper mids and the top for the bite of real brass. Mod wheel: more vibrato; aftertouch: growl. Macros: rasp, swell, bite.",
