  {
   "name": "S&H Panner",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "sequence",
   "tags": [
    "per-voice pan",
    "sample & hold",
    "tempo sync",
    "PWM"
   ],
   "description": "A per-note random LFO that takes a new value every 16th note jumps each note around the stereo field and moves its cutoff. Every note has its own random pattern, so a chord splits into independent lines, and a slower LFO per note sweeps the pulse width underneath. A little slew rounds the steps. Mod wheel: the steps go to 32nds; aftertouch: resonance. Macros: jump, filter.",
