  {
   "name": "Step Filter",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "sequence",
   "tags": [
    "sample & hold",
    "parallel filters",
    "XY random walk",
    "drive"
   ],
   "description": "After Oatmeal's filterbleh: a saw and a narrow pulse an octave up through two parallel resonant lowpasses that a stepping random LFO jumps every sixteenth (each note its own pattern), while the XY pad's random walk wanders both cutoffs, into a heavy asymmetric drive and an irregular chorus. Mod wheel: thirty-second steps; aftertouch: resonance. Macros: steps, wander, drive.",
