   ],
   "description": "A chiptune arpeggio: hold a chord and the arpeggiator runs up it in sixteenths, each note then its octave. Every step gets its own pulse duty (12.5, 25, 50 % and in between), a quick chip-style vibrato comes in with the mod wheel, and notes spread by pitch. Aftertouch: a wider duty. Macros: duty, echo.",
