  {
   "name": "Whoosh",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "fx",
   "tags": [
    "noise",
    "XY random walk",
    "resonant",
    "sweep"
   ],
   "description": "After Oatmeal's whoosh: resonant noise through a resonant lowpass swept by a per-note LFO, whose depth and speed the XY pad's random walk keeps changing, while a random LFO pans it and also modulates the sweep. Each whoosh swells open over a second and a half, harder notes further, and the drive grows with it. Mod wheel: faster wandering; aftertouch: brighter. Macros: sweep, wander.",
