  {
   "name": "Clap Stack",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "drums",
   "tags": [
    "clap",
    "noise",
    "bandpass",
    "room"
   ],
   "description": "A clap: bandpassed noise that a fast square LFO chops into a flurry of hands for the first few tens of milliseconds, then a tail, into a small room. Each clap's flurry spacing, tone and place are a little different, and harder hits are brighter. Macros: tone, room.",
